-- title:
--   Vanishing of r-old parabolic eigenclasses killed by both trace maps
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $N \ge 1$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$ and $r \nmid N$. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $N$ $2$ $S$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to $F$, subject to $\chi(T_r)^2 \ne (r+1)^2$ and to the existence of a prime $\ell_0 \ne r$ with $\ell_0 \nmid N$, $\ell_0 \notin S$ and $\chi(T_{\ell_0}) \ne \ell_0 + 1$. Let `h₁` and `hr'` be witnesses of [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) $N$ $(Nr)$ $\top$ $\top$ $d$ for $d = 1$ and $d = r$, that is, of $N \mid Nr$ together with $d \mid Nr/N$ (the condition on the unit subgroups being vacuous for $\top$). Let $c$ be an additive homomorphism from `Additive` of [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $(Nr)$ $\top$, i.e. of $\Gamma_0(Nr) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, to $F$, which is parabolic in the sense that $c(\gamma) = 0$ whenever $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$, and which satisfies [`CohCarrier.heckeT`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) $(Nr)$ $\top$ $\ell$ $c = \chi(T_\ell) \cdot c$ for every prime $\ell \ne r$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, the operator being the transfer of $c$ along [`CohCarrier.conjL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L228). If the two corestriction (trace) maps [`CohCarrier.jDeg`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L482) attached to `h₁` and to `hr'` both send $c$ to $0$, then $c = 0$.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the analysis of the auxiliary prime $r$ in the Taylor–Wiles method: on the $r$-old part of the parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ the pair of degeneracy trace maps to level $N$ is injective once the level-$N$ eigenvalue $a_r$ satisfies $a_r^2 \ne (r+1)^2$. It is used by [`CohCarrier.eq_zero_of_mem_parabolicHoms_gammaZero_auxLevel_of_heckeT_eq_smul_of_jDeg_eq_zero`](thm.html#CohCarrier.eq_zero_of_mem_parabolicHoms_gammaZero_auxLevel_of_heckeT_eq_smul_of_jDeg_eq_zero) and by [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.toML_eq_zero_of_jDeg_one_eq_zero_of_jDeg_eq_zero`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.toML_eq_zero_of_jDeg_one_eq_zero_of_jDeg_eq_zero).
